<title>CANADA: Canada raising top grain freight rates by two pct.</title>
<headline>Canada raising top grain freight rates by two pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Transportation Agency issued on Friday the maximum rate scale for rail movement of western grain for crop year 1997-98.</p>
<p>The maximum rates, which take effect on August 1, will increase two percent. For a typical movement of 1,026-1,050 miles, it said, the new rate for a tonne of grain will be C$34.78 compared with the current C$34.09.</p>
<p>These rates apply to the movement of grain from prairie elevators to terminals at Vancouver, Prince Rupert, Thunder Bay and Churchill.</p>
<p>Railway companies and shippers may negotiate lower rates when, for example, a shipper is able to load many cars within a short time at one location.</p>
<p>((Randall Palmer, Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
</text>
